WEBVTT

00:00:02.440 --> 00:00:06.650
<b>GUNDAM
VICTORY
MOBILE SUIT</b>

00:00:06.650 --> 00:00:12.610
The furious rain, Makes my heart shake
hageshii ame ga, kokoro wo yuruwaseru

00:00:12.610 --> 00:00:15.820
Like it did on that day
Ano hi no youni

00:00:17.780 --> 00:00:22.910
But I just ran through, In my dream I had till yesterday
Tada hashirinuketa, kinou made no MY DREAM

00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:26.710
...I still believe
...shinjiteiru no sa

00:00:29.550 --> 00:00:34.470
I'm willing to fight, An endless defense
Owari no nai, defense demo ii yo

00:00:35.090 --> 00:00:42.350
As long as you, Keep on gazing at me
Kimi ga boku wo, mitsumetsuzukete kureru nara

00:00:42.730 --> 00:00:45.270
STAND UP TO THE VICTORY!

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:50.980
Turn to face all the mornings ahead, And someday
Ikutsumono asa wo mukae, Itsuka kitto

00:00:52.070 --> 00:00:53.860
Try to seize them
tsukande miseru

00:00:53.990 --> 00:00:56.450
STAND UP TO THE VICTORY!

00:00:56.780 --> 00:01:02.120
Even if nothing, Lies on the other side
Sono mukougawa ni, nanimonakutemo

00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:06.040
It doesn't matter to me
kamawanai kara

00:01:06.210 --> 00:01:14.050
...Just as long as I can embrace, Your gentle, irreplaceable smile!
Kakegae no nai, kimi no yasashii egao daite

00:01:28.660 --> 00:01:31.800
In order to protect the shuttle from space dust,

00:01:31.960 --> 00:01:35.030
Üso went out for the first time into the vacuum of space.

00:01:36.030 --> 00:01:39.300
There, he met an enemy pilot who was cast away in space.

00:01:40.760 --> 00:01:44.430
Even when people are confident they can reach an understanding,

00:01:44.700 --> 00:01:47.700
when they meet a possibly dangerous enemy,

00:01:47.930 --> 00:01:49.600
they tremble in fear.

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:54.700
REINEFORCE, LIFT OFF

00:01:54.700 --> 00:01:57.630
"Reineforce, Lift Off".
REINEFORCE, LIFT OFF

00:01:57.630 --> 00:01:57.660
REINEFORCE, LIFT OFF

00:02:10.730 --> 00:02:12.660
A BESPA warship is approaching?

00:02:12.800 --> 00:02:13.930
Did they spot us?

00:02:14.230 --> 00:02:15.930
It's headed towards us.

00:02:16.560 --> 00:02:19.930
But, what's a Zanscare Empire warship...

00:02:19.960 --> 00:02:22.730
...doing at the Hiland solar battery?

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:48.260
This way!

00:02:49.360 --> 00:02:50.460
Wait!

00:02:53.730 --> 00:02:54.960
We'll hide in here.

00:02:55.600 --> 00:02:59.060
I can't believe we're doing this. You're the best sister ever, Shahkti!

00:03:00.960 --> 00:03:02.700
We've made it, Lieutenant.

00:03:03.060 --> 00:03:07.460
Looks like working all night to complete these Galguyus paid off.

00:03:07.930 --> 00:03:11.160
Would have preferred to come in the Galicsons, though.

00:03:11.630 --> 00:03:13.430
Shall we fire the torpedoes?

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:18.630
So, the military's making an exception and treating this as paid leave...

00:03:18.660 --> 00:03:23.130
...so that we can join with the League Militaire and go into space.

00:03:23.160 --> 00:03:24.100
Lieutenant Gomez.

00:03:24.130 --> 00:03:26.700
Ah, the survivors of Bagley Team.

00:03:27.330 --> 00:03:28.830
I'm Juca Meilasch.

00:03:28.860 --> 00:03:31.860
Thank you for allowing us to join you on the Reineforce.

00:03:32.300 --> 00:03:34.400
It's just an old local forces ship.

00:03:34.630 --> 00:03:37.100
We're just happy to get some payback against BESPA.

00:03:37.300 --> 00:03:38.430
That's fine.

00:03:38.460 --> 00:03:42.960
The League Militaire have supplied the Gun EZ, Victory, and other mobile suits.

00:03:43.160 --> 00:03:45.030
We need lots of pilots.

00:03:45.060 --> 00:03:47.630
What about the young genius pilot who was using the Victory?

00:03:47.730 --> 00:03:52.200
I'm afraid the little kid went into space to look for his folks.

00:03:52.830 --> 00:03:53.830
Little kid?

00:03:59.660 --> 00:04:01.200
Üso, wait!

00:04:01.400 --> 00:04:04.230
But, enemy mobile suits are coming, right?

00:04:04.300 --> 00:04:08.230
It'd be a wasted effort. Have you forgotten that we're in space?

00:04:08.260 --> 00:04:09.230
Here they come!

00:04:12.760 --> 00:04:15.630
It's a corporation shuttle, but that mobile suit...

00:04:16.360 --> 00:04:18.760
This mobile suit is fully equipped!

00:04:18.960 --> 00:04:22.930
This is BESPA patrol ship Sinope 321! Prepare for inspection!

00:04:28.530 --> 00:04:29.660
Over there?

00:04:29.800 --> 00:04:31.730
Fine, but can you open it?

00:04:33.560 --> 00:04:36.360
Wow, this ship's so old.

00:04:36.400 --> 00:04:37.530
It opened!

00:04:37.700 --> 00:04:39.630
Where are our rooms?

00:04:39.700 --> 00:04:42.260
The guest rooms should be around here.

00:04:46.430 --> 00:04:49.530
The VIP suite's looking pretty low-rent, huh?

00:04:49.560 --> 00:04:51.530
And it smells musty in here too, Kuffu.

00:04:54.660 --> 00:04:55.930
They're gone.

00:04:56.500 --> 00:04:57.760
Goodbye!

00:04:57.800 --> 00:04:59.630
Safe travels!

00:05:05.760 --> 00:05:07.330
The fleet has left.

00:05:07.400 --> 00:05:10.060
Even if the torpedoes fail, we can fight them with mobile suits.

00:05:10.400 --> 00:05:11.330
I know.

00:05:12.800 --> 00:05:14.560
Renda, open fire!

00:05:20.300 --> 00:05:23.600
I land on Earth just to head right back out into space.

00:05:26.260 --> 00:05:28.760
Missiles? No, torpedoes!

00:05:31.530 --> 00:05:34.100
One hit, but the lead ship is...

00:05:34.130 --> 00:05:34.630
Renda!

00:05:34.660 --> 00:05:35.260
Yes?

00:05:35.300 --> 00:05:37.030
Can you charge them at close range...

00:05:37.060 --> 00:05:38.600
...while firing torpedoes?

00:05:38.630 --> 00:05:40.100
I was hoping you'd ask.

00:05:40.360 --> 00:05:43.260
Everyone who aids the League Militaire will die here!

00:05:43.500 --> 00:05:45.500
Send out any mobile suits that can move!

00:05:45.530 --> 00:05:47.430
Machine guns, prep for antisubmarine combat!

00:05:47.460 --> 00:05:48.060
Yes, sir!

00:05:48.260 --> 00:05:50.660
Junko, which is my mobile suit?

00:05:50.900 --> 00:05:52.900
If it moves, you can use it!

00:05:53.730 --> 00:05:55.330
It's shakey, Shahkti!

00:05:55.360 --> 00:05:57.630
Yeah, and noisy, too.

00:06:01.530 --> 00:06:03.700
Let me show you the spirit of a biker!

00:06:15.100 --> 00:06:16.860
I won't let you get into space!

00:06:28.460 --> 00:06:30.960
The beams are completely useless in water!

00:06:45.800 --> 00:06:51.000
Renda!

00:06:56.200 --> 00:06:59.000
Lieutenant, I can't get near their main ship!

00:06:59.300 --> 00:07:02.830
We got two of their tug boats. I'm sure they can't take off, now!

00:07:03.300 --> 00:07:04.430
You're not hurt, are you?

00:07:10.560 --> 00:07:13.360
Signal from tugboat number 2.

00:07:13.700 --> 00:07:17.500
It says, "Godspeed to Lt. Gomez as captain."

00:07:18.200 --> 00:07:20.500
After I didn't even want to come here!

00:07:20.530 --> 00:07:24.230
Lieutenant, tugboat number 1 is moving off.

00:07:29.400 --> 00:07:30.730
We've cleared the hurdle!

00:07:30.830 --> 00:07:34.230
We can still clear the water's surface, even with just one tugboat!

00:07:34.260 --> 00:07:38.560
Yes. This is a spacecraft that helped forge an era!

00:07:38.600 --> 00:07:42.730
An old relic knows old relics the best, huh?

00:07:47.860 --> 00:07:51.400
All right! All hands to flight stations! We're taking off!

00:07:55.330 --> 00:07:57.460
We're helpless, and they grow stronger...

00:07:57.500 --> 00:07:59.400
Lieutenant, are you all right?

00:07:59.430 --> 00:08:02.200
S-Sorry. Can you give me a boost from below?

00:08:03.500 --> 00:08:04.830
Lieutenant, are you leaking?

00:08:04.860 --> 00:08:06.630
I'm fine. Go.

00:08:06.660 --> 00:08:07.330
Right.

00:08:09.000 --> 00:08:12.030
Suzy! This ship's already flying!

00:08:12.060 --> 00:08:15.600
That's why... we have to put these on!

00:08:27.260 --> 00:08:30.800
All hands to space flight stations. Commence onboard pressurization check.

00:08:30.830 --> 00:08:33.660
We don't have our full compliment of mobile suits.

00:08:33.700 --> 00:08:35.500
With this one warship,

00:08:35.600 --> 00:08:38.460
we're going to stop BESPA's attack on the Earth?

00:08:38.660 --> 00:08:41.100
That's our job, isn't it?

00:08:42.860 --> 00:08:44.500
Karl, are you all right?

00:08:49.730 --> 00:08:52.300
Are there any survivors in there?

00:08:52.500 --> 00:08:53.830
Doesn't look like it.

00:08:54.500 --> 00:08:57.130
Bagley Team held out for a while,

00:08:57.560 --> 00:09:01.800
but it was wiped out by the Keilas Guilie Fleet in geosynchronous orbit.

00:09:06.230 --> 00:09:10.200
She said it was just equipment! The League Militaire forced us!

00:09:10.230 --> 00:09:12.330
I had no choice!

00:09:12.660 --> 00:09:16.230
What about the Gundam replica on your payload deck?

00:09:16.260 --> 00:09:17.800
I don't know anything about it!

00:09:17.830 --> 00:09:22.130
Maybe a League Militaire warship is going to come and retrieve it!

00:09:22.660 --> 00:09:26.830
You're saying you used a mobile suit you were given to carry?

00:09:26.960 --> 00:09:29.600
We ran into some debris and had no choice.

00:09:29.630 --> 00:09:32.530
We were looking for something to use and discovered what the freight was!

00:09:32.560 --> 00:09:34.800
And used it to clear the debris?

00:09:34.830 --> 00:09:36.300
Something wrong with that?!

00:09:36.400 --> 00:09:37.900
You piloted it?

00:09:37.930 --> 00:09:38.760
Yes.

00:09:40.100 --> 00:09:42.500
I'm confiscating that mobile suit.

00:09:44.430 --> 00:09:45.900
Where are you taking it?

00:09:46.230 --> 00:09:47.360
That's a secret.

00:09:48.060 --> 00:09:51.200
Are you taking it to the area that looks like it had a battle?

00:09:52.460 --> 00:09:54.760
You saw that battle?

00:09:58.430 --> 00:10:00.300
I'm confiscating this shuttle!

00:10:00.400 --> 00:10:02.430
That's against international law!

00:10:02.600 --> 00:10:06.200
So is a PCST shuttle transporting weaponry!

00:10:10.500 --> 00:10:11.530
Are you holding on?

00:10:12.130 --> 00:10:13.730
Keep your hands on that rope.

00:10:14.130 --> 00:10:14.830
Go.

00:10:14.860 --> 00:10:15.630
Sir.

00:10:25.130 --> 00:10:27.830
This is a copy of that Gundam!

00:10:27.860 --> 00:10:31.600
The resistance is trying to use the legend of the Gundam, now?

00:10:39.330 --> 00:10:40.300
What's wrong?

00:10:41.260 --> 00:10:42.430
Get in the cabin.

00:10:42.460 --> 00:10:45.030
Sorry, I'm not used to space yet.

00:10:45.460 --> 00:10:48.700
Why'd a kid like you pick now to come up here?

00:10:50.260 --> 00:10:52.800
I'm trying to find my parents.

00:10:54.460 --> 00:10:55.730
I hope you do.

00:10:55.760 --> 00:10:56.430
Yes, sir.

00:10:56.460 --> 00:10:57.930
Secure everyone to their seats.

00:10:57.960 --> 00:11:00.460
What happens if I'm taken prisoner?

00:11:01.330 --> 00:11:02.160
Mom...

00:11:02.200 --> 00:11:03.530
Hey! Get over here!

00:11:04.030 --> 00:11:05.160
Y-Yes, sir!

00:11:12.600 --> 00:11:13.660
A ball!

00:11:13.700 --> 00:11:14.830
You from Earth?

00:11:14.860 --> 00:11:18.230
Huh? Yeah. What are you doing here?

00:11:29.400 --> 00:11:31.600
Are you from the Zanscare Empire?

00:11:31.630 --> 00:11:32.500
No way.

00:11:32.530 --> 00:11:33.300
Are you?

00:11:33.330 --> 00:11:35.160
Kids should keep quiet!

00:11:35.430 --> 00:11:38.030
We kids can talk to each other, can't we?!

00:11:38.200 --> 00:11:40.730
If you weren't a kid, you'd be tasting my fist!

00:11:40.800 --> 00:11:43.100
And don't try undoing that rope, lady!

00:11:43.400 --> 00:11:46.330
How can I when you've got my hands tied behind me?

00:11:46.600 --> 00:11:50.330
Ernest, once I get the shuttle turned around, we'll link up with a wire.

00:11:50.560 --> 00:11:52.930
Then we'll put the adults in here and the others over there.

00:11:52.960 --> 00:11:54.300
Roger that, Captain.

00:11:54.700 --> 00:11:56.400
Where are you from on Earth?

00:11:56.430 --> 00:11:57.500
Europe.

00:11:57.530 --> 00:12:00.630
I'm Warren Trace. What's your name?

00:12:00.660 --> 00:12:02.230
Martina Klánský.

00:12:02.400 --> 00:12:03.860
Odelo Henrik.

00:12:04.660 --> 00:12:06.830
And that kid's Üso Ewin.

00:12:07.900 --> 00:12:08.760
I'm Üso!

00:12:08.800 --> 00:12:10.600
I'm Karel Masaryk.

00:12:13.360 --> 00:12:15.360
Birdlime and air guns...

00:12:15.930 --> 00:12:17.860
What? Brasta is only six?

00:12:18.160 --> 00:12:20.930
What's a child like that doing on a BESPA ship?

00:12:21.360 --> 00:12:24.260
BESPA came to use the solar power satellite we live on for something,

00:12:24.300 --> 00:12:26.700
so they took us hostage.

00:12:27.100 --> 00:12:28.230
Hostage?

00:12:28.400 --> 00:12:32.930
They took us with them to make our dads do what they wanted!

00:12:33.800 --> 00:12:36.030
I want to go home.

00:12:37.500 --> 00:12:38.430
Üso...

00:12:39.060 --> 00:12:39.960
Odelo.

00:12:41.830 --> 00:12:44.830
Hey, Üso, what are you thinking?

00:12:45.660 --> 00:12:47.530
We'll use the shuttle's thrust, too.

00:12:47.560 --> 00:12:49.560
Unit two says it's en route.

00:12:50.400 --> 00:12:54.000
Please, use Haro's ears. Haro, raise your ears!

00:12:58.330 --> 00:13:00.960
What? With the birdlime and wires?

00:13:01.000 --> 00:13:03.330
It should work. The rest is all in the timing.

00:13:03.800 --> 00:13:04.900
Right, Karel?

00:13:05.200 --> 00:13:07.960
I can also use pesticide and the signal flares.

00:13:08.060 --> 00:13:11.660
For the two in the pilot's seats and the two mobile suit pilots...

00:13:12.130 --> 00:13:14.960
If we split them up, we can take the shuttle.

00:13:17.800 --> 00:13:19.560
The mobile suits have docked?

00:13:19.800 --> 00:13:20.800
Üso!

00:13:20.830 --> 00:13:21.560
Right.

00:13:25.960 --> 00:13:27.330
Anything you want?

00:13:27.600 --> 00:13:29.130
I... I want my mom!

00:13:29.160 --> 00:13:30.700
How old are you?

00:13:31.560 --> 00:13:33.030
I want to go home!

00:13:33.060 --> 00:13:35.060
I'll give you some candy later.

00:13:41.430 --> 00:13:44.330
Here, kid. Candy. Eat up!

00:13:45.460 --> 00:13:47.860
When can I go back to my mom?

00:13:47.900 --> 00:13:48.900
Soon.

00:13:49.460 --> 00:13:50.830
Keep quiet.

00:13:51.460 --> 00:13:52.260
Right.

00:13:53.300 --> 00:13:54.400
Look out!

00:13:55.700 --> 00:13:56.600
Haro, wait!

00:13:56.630 --> 00:13:58.000
What's the problem?

00:13:58.100 --> 00:13:59.430
Grab Haro!

00:13:59.460 --> 00:14:00.730
The air gun's power is...

00:14:00.760 --> 00:14:02.130
What?

00:14:04.560 --> 00:14:08.000
Misaki! What's happening?! Are you trying to resist?!

00:14:08.030 --> 00:14:09.260
Why, you!

00:14:10.430 --> 00:14:11.560
Don't cry.

00:14:11.600 --> 00:14:12.630
Head for the shuttle.

00:14:12.660 --> 00:14:15.200
Üso, Odelo, Karel! Get back!

00:14:15.560 --> 00:14:15.960
Odelo!

00:14:16.030 --> 00:14:17.160
Misaki, can't you move?!

00:14:17.200 --> 00:14:17.660
Stop!

00:14:17.700 --> 00:14:21.960
Why, you... We treat you nice, and this is what we get?! Unforgivable!

00:14:22.130 --> 00:14:23.130
You...

00:14:23.400 --> 00:14:24.300
Haro!

00:14:26.800 --> 00:14:28.860
Why are they using pesticide?!

00:14:29.030 --> 00:14:30.160
I'll kill them!

00:14:30.200 --> 00:14:31.930
Are you serious? We're in a ship!

00:14:32.800 --> 00:14:36.160
Use Victory to cut the wire connecting this ship to the shuttle!

00:14:36.200 --> 00:14:37.100
Right!

00:14:45.800 --> 00:14:47.930
Warren, can you use the air gun?

00:14:47.960 --> 00:14:48.700
I can!

00:14:48.730 --> 00:14:50.130
We've found the shuttle.

00:14:52.500 --> 00:14:53.660
What's wrong?

00:14:54.600 --> 00:14:56.400
Press that button more gently!

00:14:57.430 --> 00:14:59.430
Martina, wait!

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:01.030
Can you use the air gun?

00:15:01.060 --> 00:15:01.930
Yeah!

00:15:01.960 --> 00:15:02.930
Odelo!

00:15:02.960 --> 00:15:05.760
Huh? Where are they? Wait!

00:15:07.800 --> 00:15:09.260
Use it on the mobile suit!

00:15:09.500 --> 00:15:11.230
So they can't open the hatch.

00:15:11.260 --> 00:15:12.160
Roger!

00:15:12.430 --> 00:15:13.460
W-Wait!

00:15:13.500 --> 00:15:14.430
Captain!

00:15:15.700 --> 00:15:16.800
Got it!

00:15:18.300 --> 00:15:19.300
Hurry!

00:15:19.330 --> 00:15:21.460
The enemy's coming out of the other hatch!

00:15:22.160 --> 00:15:23.430
The forward airlock!

00:15:23.660 --> 00:15:25.560
That tube was an airlock?!

00:15:27.500 --> 00:15:28.300
Odelo!

00:15:28.330 --> 00:15:29.630
S-Sorry!

00:15:30.260 --> 00:15:32.900
Üso, do you read me? Deal with them!

00:15:32.930 --> 00:15:34.500
Hang on! I'll be there soon!

00:15:35.060 --> 00:15:37.400
Once again, I have to depend on Üso!

00:15:38.260 --> 00:15:39.830
Set your air gun to maximum power!

00:15:42.130 --> 00:15:44.600
I can't cut the wires with the barrier!

00:15:44.960 --> 00:15:46.860
Why does nothing on this thing work?!

00:15:47.000 --> 00:15:48.630
Captain Genis, I'm moving out!

00:15:48.660 --> 00:15:50.360
It looks like the enemy is deploying their mobile suit, as well!

00:15:58.530 --> 00:16:00.630
Miss Marbet, I'm using the rifle!

00:16:00.660 --> 00:16:01.530
Go ahead.

00:16:02.230 --> 00:16:04.330
Odelo's in the shuttle now, too!

00:16:06.830 --> 00:16:08.100
I can't hit them!

00:16:10.130 --> 00:16:11.760
Can't you board the Zoloat?

00:16:12.130 --> 00:16:13.700
I can't get in from outside.

00:16:16.530 --> 00:16:17.960
Damn wires!

00:16:18.800 --> 00:16:20.200
Sorry, sir.

00:16:20.230 --> 00:16:22.100
There's not much you can do about birdlime.

00:16:28.200 --> 00:16:29.000
Captain...

00:16:29.030 --> 00:16:31.460
That boy Üso is amazing.

00:16:31.930 --> 00:16:34.130
He's using his unit to help us turn.

00:16:34.160 --> 00:16:37.300
His handling and thruster use is among the best I've seen.

00:16:37.330 --> 00:16:39.600
But how are we going to escape?

00:16:39.960 --> 00:16:41.360
We'll figure something out.

00:16:43.030 --> 00:16:44.260
It's moving.

00:16:51.400 --> 00:16:53.230
Pesticide in here, too?!

00:16:54.930 --> 00:16:57.130
I won't let you catch up with us!

00:17:02.900 --> 00:17:03.900
He's gone!

00:17:05.600 --> 00:17:08.460
I don't care if you're civilians or part of the corporation!

00:17:16.530 --> 00:17:18.100
What is this power?!

00:17:18.300 --> 00:17:20.530
It's nothing like the Federation's mobile suits!

00:17:21.960 --> 00:17:23.700
If I get a direct hit,

00:17:23.730 --> 00:17:26.830
the explosion might take out the shuttle and the BESPA ship!

00:17:30.530 --> 00:17:32.460
Are you better than the Bagley Team?

00:17:37.530 --> 00:17:38.960
It takes more than that!

00:17:39.030 --> 00:17:43.100
You think someone fresh off of Earth can beat a Zoloat here in space?!

00:17:45.360 --> 00:17:46.260
What?!

00:17:47.900 --> 00:17:50.460
A beam? A different kind of beam!

00:17:50.900 --> 00:17:52.730
But there should be only one unit!

00:17:54.400 --> 00:17:56.660
From above?! But the enemy's straight in front of me!

00:17:57.000 --> 00:17:58.660
Üso's having a tough fight, isn't he?

00:17:58.700 --> 00:18:01.400
That kid's piloting the white mobile suit?

00:18:01.430 --> 00:18:03.700
Yeah. Üso's not normal.

00:18:04.500 --> 00:18:08.700
He's the same age as me. He might be a Newtype!

00:18:09.360 --> 00:18:11.000
Marbet! Where are you going?

00:18:11.030 --> 00:18:12.500
To the payload cabin.

00:18:12.530 --> 00:18:14.600
I'll give him some support with the Gundam's spare weapons.

00:18:14.730 --> 00:18:15.530
I'll help!

00:18:15.560 --> 00:18:16.660
Me, too!

00:18:17.060 --> 00:18:18.830
We're going back there?

00:18:19.130 --> 00:18:20.060
You gonna help?

00:18:20.260 --> 00:18:23.160
I don't know anything about the weapons on this shuttle.

00:18:23.330 --> 00:18:26.360
Another mobile suit might show up, right?

00:18:26.830 --> 00:18:28.230
If it does...

00:18:31.000 --> 00:18:34.160
It doesn't matter. That Üso Ewin kid will be all right.

00:18:34.830 --> 00:18:36.330
He's no Newtype.

00:18:36.460 --> 00:18:38.330
He's just a normal kid who grew up on Earth.

00:18:41.260 --> 00:18:43.130
The enemy... is here!

00:18:45.030 --> 00:18:48.460
If the Zoloat's strings tricked you, then you're mine!

00:18:48.600 --> 00:18:50.560
Trying to trap me in your beams?!

00:18:54.530 --> 00:18:56.330
He's trying to pin me down!

00:18:56.360 --> 00:18:58.360
Payback for making fools of us!

00:19:00.560 --> 00:19:01.500
I did it!

00:19:02.260 --> 00:19:04.200
You think that could beat me?!

00:19:11.960 --> 00:19:15.500
Please open the hatch! Or else I'll cut it open with my beam!

00:19:15.900 --> 00:19:18.630
If I have to do that, you'll be burned alive.

00:19:20.960 --> 00:19:23.030
I'll open it! Please don't shoot!

00:19:28.930 --> 00:19:31.900
Pilot, please put your hands up and move out onto the hatch.

00:19:35.530 --> 00:19:38.700
Okay, any funny moves, and I dump you out!

00:19:41.200 --> 00:19:42.500
It's just the legs?!

00:19:42.830 --> 00:19:45.060
He tricked me by separating?!

00:19:45.630 --> 00:19:47.500
You son of a...

00:19:47.960 --> 00:19:49.700
I said not to move!

00:19:52.600 --> 00:19:55.230
Why do they only think about fighting?

00:20:06.530 --> 00:20:08.800
You... You're saving me?

00:20:09.300 --> 00:20:13.560
I'm using you to ensure that you guys don't attack us kids again!

00:20:15.100 --> 00:20:16.500
"Us kids?"

00:20:16.930 --> 00:20:19.200
That voice... It's a child's voice!

00:20:20.200 --> 00:20:22.960
Captain Hus, I've spotted Henry!

00:20:23.260 --> 00:20:25.860
He's alive and being held by the Gundam replica.

00:20:26.260 --> 00:20:28.900
Henry's alive? Where's the Zoloat?

00:20:29.230 --> 00:20:31.200
Looks like the PCST shuttle got it.

00:20:31.500 --> 00:20:32.600
Do I attack?

00:20:32.830 --> 00:20:35.100
Can you take Henry back and win?

00:20:35.260 --> 00:20:37.400
I... I doubt it, sir.

00:20:37.730 --> 00:20:39.860
Oh, this blasted wire!

00:20:54.100 --> 00:20:57.630
This was the League Militaire's idea. The PCST has no involvement.

00:20:57.800 --> 00:20:59.300
I can see that.

00:20:59.360 --> 00:21:03.660
But you understand there'll be a high price to pay for this, right?

00:21:03.830 --> 00:21:06.730
Until the guillotine-using Zanscare Empire is crushed,

00:21:06.760 --> 00:21:08.760
we're prepared for anything!

00:21:09.030 --> 00:21:11.760
Ideologues of every age say that.

00:21:12.130 --> 00:21:15.000
But I can't forgive your involving children in this!

00:21:16.500 --> 00:21:18.360
I understand what you're saying,

00:21:18.400 --> 00:21:20.930
but to stop the guillotines from being used,

00:21:20.960 --> 00:21:22.300
we have no choice!

00:21:22.830 --> 00:21:24.660
I understand what you're saying, too.

00:21:25.330 --> 00:21:27.300
Please release Henry.

00:21:28.030 --> 00:21:32.130
Üso, when he touches the Zoloat, release the pilot.

00:21:32.160 --> 00:21:33.030
Right.

00:21:33.560 --> 00:21:34.900
Misaki, we're going back.

00:21:34.930 --> 00:21:35.730
Yes, sir!

00:21:36.960 --> 00:21:38.100
Be careful.

00:21:38.460 --> 00:21:40.360
I appreciate it, kid.

00:21:40.900 --> 00:21:46.130
And tell the captain, "Thank you for treating us kindly."

00:22:11.560 --> 00:22:12.660
Üso...

00:22:13.730 --> 00:22:15.760
Are you out there?

00:22:24.060 --> 00:22:29.530
Piercing the sky, Blue lightning
sora wo tsukisasu aoi inazuma

00:22:29.530 --> 00:22:35.320
Staining the earth, With the shadow of greed
daichi o someteku, yokubou no kage

00:22:36.370 --> 00:22:41.460
Once again, when the nightmare, Envelops the Earth
futatabi akumu ga, sekai wo tsutsumu toki

00:22:41.460 --> 00:22:46.790
You hear voices crying out "S.O.S."
"SOS" wo sakebu koe ga kikoeru...

00:22:48.630 --> 00:22:54.130
Let proud hope fill your heart
hokoritakaki kibou wo mune ni

00:22:54.720 --> 00:23:03.100
And stand up! Say a prayer for peace!!
tachiagare! heiwa no inori komete!

00:23:04.100 --> 00:23:05.100
WINNERS FOREVER!

00:23:06.100 --> 00:23:08.980
In every age
itsuno jidai mo

00:23:08.980 --> 00:23:14.570
...People take risks for freedom
hito wa jiyuu wo kakete

00:23:15.000 --> 00:23:17.000
WINNERS FOREVER!

00:23:18.330 --> 00:23:21.240
The battle goes on
tatakai tsuzukeru

00:23:21.240 --> 00:23:25.920
Fighting all alone in solitude
kodoku na made ni hitori...

00:23:34.500 --> 00:23:38.630
The colony near the moon that is visible from Kasarelia...

00:23:39.130 --> 00:23:41.700
There, the Queen of the Zanscare Empire...

00:23:41.760 --> 00:23:45.460
...cheers her soldiers on and spurs them to war.

00:23:46.400 --> 00:23:49.660
But what sort of person is the queen?

00:23:51.200 --> 00:23:53.930
Next time, on Mobile Suit Victory Gundam:

00:23:53.960 --> 00:23:56.900
Next Episode QUEEN OF THE EMPIRE
"Queen of the Empire".

00:23:56.900 --> 00:23:58.260
Please watch it!

00:23:58.260 --> 00:23:59.900
Next Episode QUEEN OF THE EMPIRE
